        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Well, I understand what you mean. It's different with everyone's habits. I personally like to find the character that needs to be replaced first and replace it there. So I expect you to consider whether to provide a configuration to automatically select whether to automatically manipulate the character under the current cursor\r\n\r\nWith current approach there is no need to manually find which surrounding will be replaced. It is taken care of by appropriate searching of surrounding user wants to replace.\r\n\r\nThe approach of automatically inferring surrounding id with character under cursor leads to plenty of problems down the road. Besides mentioned use case earlier, it disables possibility to replace surrounding with more than a single character parts (like function call, tag, etc.).\r\n\r\nSo no, unfortunately, I don't see this as a part of 'mini.surround'.",
